        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: परिवेषयति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "परिवेषयति — pariveṣayati — \"serves food\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माता अतिथये भोजनं परिवेषयति। mātā atithaye bhojanaṃ pariveṣayati. Mother serves food to the guest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (she …): सा ओदनं परिवेषितवती, sā odanaṃ pariveṣitavatī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "परिवेषयति (pariveṣayati) is built on pari, \"around\", and the root √viṣ, \"to be active, to work\"; MW gives pariviṣ as to serve, to wait on, to offer or dress food (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
